From: Harman Bagrah <harmanbagrah.dev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: enable AP+STA concurrent mode for RTL8821C

The rtw88 driver currently only advertises iface_combinations
(allowing simultaneous STA + AP virtual interfaces on one radio) for
the RTW_CHIP_TYPE_8822C chip. The RTL8821C chip, which shares the
same core hardware/firmware architecture, has this capability gated
out entirely, causing `iw list` to report "interface combinations
are not supported" and preventing any concurrent STA+AP (e.g.
hotspot-while-connected) use case on this otherwise-common laptop
WiFi chip.

Realtek's own vendor SDK for this chip family (used in embedded and
Android products) ships with concurrent mode as a standard, widely
enabled build option (CONFIG_CONCURRENT_MODE appears in nearly every
platform profile in the vendor Makefile), suggesting the underlying
firmware supports this operation and the gap is specifically in the
upstream Linux driver's capability advertisement, not the hardware.

Tested on a Dell Inspiron 15 3535 (RTL8821CE, PCIe), firmware version
24.11.0 / H2C version 12. After this patch, `iw list` correctly shows:

    valid interface combinations:
         * #{ managed } <= 1, #{ AP } <= 1,
           total <= 2, #channels <= 1

Verified working end-to-end: STA interface (wlp2s0) stays associated
to an existing AP while a second AP-mode interface is created and
used to host a hotspot via hostapd + dnsmasq, on the same channel,
simultaneously, with no driver errors, warnings, or instability
observed during testing.

Signed-off-by: Harman Bagrah <harmanbagrah.dev@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
@@ -2296,7 +2296,8 @@ int rtw_register_hw(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev, struct ieee80211_hw *hw)
 	hw->wiphy->max_scan_ssids = RTW_SCAN_MAX_SSIDS;
 	hw->wiphy->max_scan_ie_len = rtw_get_max_scan_ie_len(rtwdev);
 
-	if (rtwdev->chip->id == RTW_CHIP_TYPE_8822C) {
+	if (rtwdev->chip->id == RTW_CHIP_TYPE_8822C ||
+	    rtwdev->chip->id == RTW_CHIP_TYPE_8821C) {
 		hw->wiphy->iface_combinations = rtw_iface_combs;
 		hw->wiphy->n_iface_combinations = ARRAY_SIZE(rtw_iface_combs);
 	}
--
